  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">Polycarp, bishop of Smyrna and disciple of the apostle John, wrote to the Philippians sometime in the early second century in response to their request. The letter is pastoral and practical, urging faith, patience, and almsgiving while warning against the love of money. Polycarp quotes Paul and the Gospels freely, giving us one of the earliest witnesses to the formation of the New Testament canon.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
